analyses.3:
After 84 zero trials, r2c2 scored 0.44 on dev and 0.40 on training success, with 1 seed. r2c4 scored 0.11 and r2c3 0.07. All three scoring trials have the transposed-frame footprint head. Every trial without it scored 0 (r2c5, r2c6 and all of round 1). So the world's action layout is probably transposed (x-major). r2c1 also had the transposed head and scored 0. It used a 3x3 trunk, 2 epochs and about 147k steps, so seed luck or too few samples could explain it. Training success is close to dev success, so the problem is not generalisation. The agent is still learning, so more fresh samples and more gradient steps should help.

This round stays near r2c2:
- a near-copy at a smaller width, to check it was not luck;
- one-change recipe variants: 64 minibatches, and lr 3e-3;
- a transposed-only head, which gets r≤1 and about 426k steps and also tests the layout idea;
- a transposed-only head with a shared square kernel, which still works if the footprints are swapped too;
- a stack of the first two ideas.
